---
import './figures.css';
---
<figure class="cl-figure" aria-labelledby="purchase-title">
  <figcaption id="purchase-title"><span class="cl-number">Figure 3</span> A North order still needs West’s stock</figcaption>
  <div class="cl-panel">
    <p class="cl-label">Independent replay · before purchase 103 exists</p>
    <div class="cl-card cl-active"><b>North application · one purchase transaction</b><span>Every required change must share one outcome.</span></div>
    <div class="cl-three cl-purchase-grid">
      <div class="cl-region"><strong>North · row home</strong><div class="cl-card"><b>orders + order_items</b><span>103 · pending</span><span>P7 × 1 at 20.00</span><span>P3 × 2 at 4.50</span><span>Total 29.00 · no payment</span></div></div>
      <div class="cl-arrow">⇄<br />Regional coordination</div>
      <div class="cl-region"><strong>West · table home</strong><div class="cl-card"><b>products · stock guard</b><span>P7: 1 → 0</span><span>P3: 12 → 10</span><span>Shared stock authority</span></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="cl-card"><b>Other required work</b><span>Global order-ID uniqueness · foreign-key checks · maintained indexes</span><span class="cl-small">Region prefixes do not remove these responsibilities.</span></div>
  </div>
  <p class="cl-caption">A dependency drawing of the independent purchase replay, not a native execution trace, range count or commit-message schedule. Each participant’s range replication and the transaction protocol add work. The arrow supplies no elapsed time; neither side commits a partial purchase.</p>
</figure>
<style>.cl-purchase-grid { grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) 7rem minmax(0,1fr); align-items:center; } @media(max-width:520px){.cl-purchase-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr;} .cl-purchase-grid .cl-arrow{padding:0;}}</style>
